{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 formalization of the paper 'An 83/84 approximation for three-occurrence Horn formulas above the Unique Games thresholds'. The compared results are: the three-occurrence formula T_H built from a cubic graph, its explicit clause semantics (at most one negative literal per clause, with a proved complement-variable translation to standard Horn clauses that preserves satisfaction), the exact identity OPT(T_H) = 4n + m + alpha, the repair lemma, the number of clauses and the three occurrences of every variable, and the 83/84 approximation ratio transferred from a cubic independent-set guarantee, together with the degree-d ratio arithmetic. The supporting modules also formalize the MAX-CUT reduction, the conflict graph and the lift of a Goemans-Williamson cut to the 83/84 ratio. Goemans-Williamson, Berman-Fujito and the Unique Games thresholds are cited hypotheses, not reproved.",
